Using `extractAllTo` without sanitizing entry paths can introduce zip-slip vulnerabilities. Consider validating each entry's normalized path against `destPath` or use a safe extraction method that prevents directory traversal.
```suggestion
 for (const entry of zip.getEntries()) {
 const entryPath = path.resolve(destPath, entry.entryName);
 if (!entryPath.startsWith(destPath)) {
 throw new RepomixError(`Zip entry path traversal detected: ${entry.entryName}`);
 }
 if (entry.isDirectory) {
 await fs.mkdir(entryPath, { recursive: true });
 } else {
 await fs.mkdir(path.dirname(entryPath), { recursive: true });
 await fs.writeFile(entryPath, entry.getData());
 }
 }
```

Avoid using `any` for `initialFormData`. Define a proper interface for the form data shape to improve type safety and readability.
